{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-00",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Jointly Optimized PPO Portfolio Management with a Differentiable Regime Encoder\n",
    "### Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE) — Banking Sector, 2021–2025\n",
    "\n",
    "End-to-end pipeline notebook. Runs top-to-bottom on **Colab or locally**, and calls the\n",
    "same `src/` modules as `main.py` — no reimplementation, so what you validate here is\n",
    "what runs in production.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Prices / Volumes  →  Preprocessing (features → normalize → 30-day windows)\n",
    "                                    │\n",
    "                                    │  x_t : (n_assets, 30, 15)   ← per asset\n",
    "                                    ▼\n",
    "┌──────────────── Differentiable Regime Encoder ────────────────┐\n",
    "│                                                               │\n",
    "│   V-VSN + LSTM  ──►  Temporal MHA        (shared weights,     │\n",
    "│        │                   │              applied per asset)  │\n",
    "│        └───────────────────┘                                  │\n",
    "│                    H : (B, N, d_lstm)                         │\n",
    "│                            │                                  │\n",
    "│                  Macro Graph Prior (GAT over the N assets)    │\n",
    "│                            │                                  │\n",
    "│              per-asset fusion → h_asset : (B, N, 128)         │\n",
    "│                            │                                  │\n",
    "│              mean-pool over assets → h_market : (B, 128)      │\n",
    "│                            │                                  │\n",
    "│                   Regime Classifier → p(regime) : (B, 3)      │\n",
    "└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n",
    "         │                                        │\n",
    "         │ h_asset (per asset)                    │ h_market (pooled)\n",
    "         ▼                                        ▼\n",
    "   Actor π  → weights a_t  (B, N)           Critic V → V(s)  (B,)\n",
    "         │                                        │\n",
    "         └──────────►  PPO clipped objective  ◄───┘\n",
    "                    joint end-to-end gradient update\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**What \"jointly optimized\" means here:** encoder, actor and critic are one `nn.Module`.\n",
    "A single `backward()` on `L_clip + 0.5·L_value + 0.01·L_entropy` updates the VSN, LSTM,\n",
    "MHA, GAT, fusion layer, regime classifier, actor and critic together. The regime\n",
    "classifier never sees a regime label — regimes are whatever partition of market states\n",
    "helps the portfolio objective.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Per-asset, not market-blob.** Every asset's own 30×15 window goes through the *same*\n",
    "temporal backbone (channel-independent), so the GAT operates on N genuinely distinct\n",
    "node embeddings and the actor scores each asset on its own evidence."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-01",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 1. Environment setup\n",
    "\n",
    "Detects Colab vs. local. `torch-geometric` is **not** required — the GAT in\n",
    "`src/models/macro_graph_prior.py` is written from scratch in plain PyTorch."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-02",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import sys, os, subprocess\n",
    "\n",
    "IN_COLAB = \"google.colab\" in sys.modules\n",
    "\n",
    "REQUIREMENTS = [\n",
    "    \"torch>=2.0.0\", \"numpy>=1.24.0\", \"pandas>=2.0.0\", \"scipy>=1.10.0\",\n",
    "    \"scikit-learn>=1.2.0\", \"matplotlib>=3.7.0\", \"tensorboard>=2.13.0\",\n",
    "    \"pyarrow>=12.0.0\", \"statsmodels>=0.14.0\", \"openpyxl>=3.1.0\", \"pyyaml>=6.0\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "INSTALL_DEPS = IN_COLAB          # flip to True to force a local install\n",
    "\n",
    "if INSTALL_DEPS:\n",
    "    print(\"Installing dependencies ...\")\n",
    "    subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"-q\", *REQUIREMENTS], check=True)\n",
    "    print(\"done.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Skipping install (set INSTALL_DEPS = True to run it).\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\npython  : {sys.version.split()[0]}\")\n",
    "print(f\"colab   : {IN_COLAB}\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-03",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.1 Locate the project root\n",
    "\n",
    "The notebook expects:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "<PROJECT_ROOT>/\n",
    "├── src/                        # the package\n",
    "├── data/raw/20XX_banking_sector.csv\n",
    "└── main.py\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Everything below imports from `src/`, so the root must be on `sys.path`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-04",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "if IN_COLAB:\n",
    "    # ── Option A: clone from git ───────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "    REPO_URL = \"\"                       # e.g. \"https://github.com/<user>/<repo>.git\"\n",
    "    if REPO_URL:\n",
    "        if not Path(\"/content/project\").exists():\n",
    "            subprocess.run([\"git\", \"clone\", REPO_URL, \"/content/project\"], check=True)\n",
    "        PROJECT_ROOT = Path(\"/content/project\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        # ── Option B: Google Drive ────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "        from google.colab import drive\n",
    "        drive.mount(\"/content/drive\")\n",
    "        PROJECT_ROOT = Path(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/Regime detection portfolio\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    # Walk up from the notebook until we find the package root.\n",
    "    PROJECT_ROOT = Path.cwd().resolve()\n",
    "    while not (PROJECT_ROOT / \"src\").is_dir() and PROJECT_ROOT != PROJECT_ROOT.parent:\n",
    "        PROJECT_ROOT = PROJECT_ROOT.parent\n",
    "\n",
    "assert (PROJECT_ROOT / \"src\").is_dir(), f\"src/ not found under {PROJECT_ROOT}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "os.chdir(PROJECT_ROOT)\n",
    "if str(PROJECT_ROOT) not in sys.path:\n",
    "    sys.path.insert(0, str(PROJECT_ROOT))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"PROJECT_ROOT : {PROJECT_ROOT}\")\n",
    "print(f\"raw data     : {sorted(p.name for p in (PROJECT_ROOT / 'data' / 'raw').glob('*.csv'))}\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-05",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 2. Imports, seeding, device"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-06",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "import logging\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "from datetime import datetime\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=FutureWarning)\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=UserWarning)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Project modules — same ones main.py uses ───────────────────────────\n",
    "from src.config.config import (\n",
    "    get_config, DATA_RAW_DIR, MODELS_DIR, RESULTS_DIR, FIGURES_DIR, LOGS_DIR,\n",
    ")\n",
    "from src.data.data_loader import CSEDataLoader\n",
    "from src.data.preprocessor import Preprocessor\n",
    "from src.environment.market_env import MarketEnvironment\n",
    "from src.environment.reward import RewardCalculator\n",
    "from src.models.ppo_agent import PPOAgent\n",
    "from src.training.trainer import PPOTrainer\n",
    "from src.utils.metrics import PortfolioMetrics\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def set_seed(seed: int):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Seed every RNG the pipeline touches.\"\"\"\n",
    "    np.random.seed(seed)\n",
    "    torch.manual_seed(seed)\n",
    "    if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
    "        torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(seed)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "SEED = 42\n",
    "DEVICE = \"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\n",
    "set_seed(SEED)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"torch  : {torch.__version__}\")\n",
    "print(f\"device : {DEVICE}\" + (f\"  ({torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)})\" if DEVICE == \"cuda\" else \"\"))"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-07",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.1 Plot style and training logs\n",
    "\n",
    "Two housekeeping decisions, both worth knowing about:\n",
    "\n",
    "**Charts.** One shared style: light surface, recessive grid, categorical colours assigned\n",
    "in a fixed order (blue → orange → aqua) so a series keeps its colour across every figure.\n",
    "Those three hues are colourblind-separable as a set; series are also direct-labelled or\n",
    "legended, never identified by colour alone.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Logs.** `PPOTrainer` emits an `INFO` line *per environment step* containing the full\n",
    "raw action vector — thousands of lines that would bury the notebook. The filter below\n",
    "drops exactly those and keeps the periodic progress lines."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-08",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# ── Chart style ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "SERIES = [\"#2a78d6\", \"#eb6834\", \"#1baf7a\"]      # categorical slots 1–3, fixed order\n",
    "INK, INK_MUTED, GRID = \"#0b0b0b\", \"#52514e\", \"#d8d7d2\"\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.rcParams.update({\n",
    "    \"figure.facecolor\": \"#fcfcfb\", \"axes.facecolor\": \"#fcfcfb\",\n",
    "    \"axes.edgecolor\": GRID, \"axes.labelcolor\": INK_MUTED, \"axes.titlecolor\": INK,\n",
    "    \"axes.grid\": True, \"grid.color\": GRID, \"grid.linewidth\": 0.6, \"grid.alpha\": 0.7,\n",
    "    \"axes.spines.top\": False, \"axes.spines.right\": False,\n",
    "    \"xtick.color\": INK_MUTED, \"ytick.color\": INK_MUTED,\n",
    "    \"font.size\": 10, \"axes.titlesize\": 11, \"legend.frameon\": False,\n",
    "    \"figure.dpi\": 110,\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Training log filter ────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "class _DropPerStepActions(logging.Filter):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Drop the per-step 'Train step N: raw_action=[...]' spam, keep progress.\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    def filter(self, record):\n",
    "        return not str(record.getMessage()).startswith(\"Train step\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "_handler = logging.StreamHandler(sys.stdout)\n",
    "_handler.setFormatter(logging.Formatter(\"%(asctime)s | %(message)s\", \"%H:%M:%S\"))\n",
    "_handler.addFilter(_DropPerStepActions())\n",
    "\n",
    "for _name in (\"src.training.trainer\", \"src.data.data_loader\", \"src.data.preprocessor\"):\n",
    "    _lg = logging.getLogger(_name)\n",
    "    _lg.handlers.clear()\n",
    "    _lg.addHandler(_handler)\n",
    "    _lg.setLevel(logging.INFO)\n",
    "    _lg.propagate = False\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Plot style and log handlers configured.\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-09",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 3. Configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "Every hyperparameter comes from `src/config/config.py`. Run-specific overrides live in\n",
    "this cell rather than in the config module, so the notebook stays a reproducible record\n",
    "of *one* run.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Two settings that bite if you change them carelessly:**\n",
    "\n",
    "- `EVAL_FREQUENCY` and `SAVE_FREQUENCY` must be **integer multiples of\n",
    "  `ROLLOUT_LENGTH`**. The trainer checks `global_step % eval_frequency == 0`, and\n",
    "  `global_step` advances in `rollout_length` jumps — a non-multiple means evaluation\n",
    "  never fires, so `best_model.pt` is never written and early stopping never triggers.\n",
    "- **Macro variables are disabled** (`n_macro_variables = 0`), matching `main.py`. The\n",
    "  graph prior therefore builds its adjacency over assets only."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-10",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# ── Run-level knobs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "N_ASSETS        = 47        # upper bound; the loader keeps the most complete tickers,\n",
    "                            # so the effective count (printed in §4) may be lower.\n",
    "WINDOW_SIZE     = 30        # look-back days per observation x_t. Splits happen BEFORE\n",
    "                            # windowing, so each extra look-back day costs one usable\n",
    "                            # step in every split: val/test hold 122/123 rows, so\n",
    "                            # W=30 -> 93/94 windows, W=60 -> 63/64. Practical ceiling\n",
    "                            # is ~60; by W=120 the test split is too short to score.\n",
    "                            # No model dimension depends on W (see §6 for the counts).\n",
    "TOTAL_TIMESTEPS = 20_000    # raise to 200_000+ for a run worth reporting\n",
    "ROLLOUT_LENGTH  = 256\n",
    "N_EPOCHS        = 10\n",
    "BATCH_SIZE      = 64\n",
    "LEARNING_RATE   = 3e-4\n",
    "EVAL_FREQUENCY  = 8 * ROLLOUT_LENGTH     # must be a multiple of ROLLOUT_LENGTH\n",
    "SAVE_FREQUENCY  = 40 * ROLLOUT_LENGTH    # ditto\n",
    "FORCE_RELOAD    = False     # True re-parses the raw CSVs instead of the parquet cache\n",
    "\n",
    "config = get_config(seed=SEED, device=DEVICE)\n",
    "\n",
    "config.ppo.total_timesteps  = TOTAL_TIMESTEPS\n",
    "config.ppo.rollout_length   = ROLLOUT_LENGTH\n",
    "config.ppo.n_epochs         = N_EPOCHS\n",
    "config.ppo.batch_size       = BATCH_SIZE\n",
    "config.ppo.learning_rate    = LEARNING_RATE\n",
    "config.ppo.eval_frequency   = EVAL_FREQUENCY\n",
    "config.ppo.save_frequency   = SAVE_FREQUENCY\n",
    "\n",
    "config.data.n_assets           = N_ASSETS\n",
    "config.data.window_size        = WINDOW_SIZE\n",
    "config.data.n_macro_variables  = 0     # macro disabled for this phase\n",
    "\n",
    "assert EVAL_FREQUENCY % ROLLOUT_LENGTH == 0, \"eval_frequency must be a multiple of rollout_length\"\n",
    "assert SAVE_FREQUENCY % ROLLOUT_LENGTH == 0, \"save_frequency must be a multiple of rollout_length\"\n",
    "assert 2 <= WINDOW_SIZE <= 100, \"window_size must leave enough rows for the val/test splits\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"window_size       : {config.data.window_size}\")\n",
    "print(f\"splits            : {config.data.train_ratio:.0%} / {config.data.val_ratio:.0%} / {config.data.test_ratio:.0%}\")\n",
    "print(f\"latent_state_dim  : {config.regime_encoder.latent_state_dim}\")\n",
    "print(f\"n_regimes         : {config.regime_encoder.n_regimes}\")\n",
    "print(f\"allow_short       : {config.environment.allow_short_selling}\"\n",
    "      f\"   → actor squash = {'tanh (independent per asset)' if config.environment.allow_short_selling else 'softmax (long-only simplex)'}\")\n",
    "print(f\"vol_target        : {config.environment.vol_target}  (only active when allow_short)\")\n",
    "print(f\"max_position_size : {config.environment.max_position_size:.0%}\")\n",
    "print(f\"rollouts to run   : {TOTAL_TIMESTEPS // ROLLOUT_LENGTH}\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-11",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 4. Data loading\n",
    "\n",
    "`CSEDataLoader` reads each yearly banking-sector CSV (detecting the header row, which\n",
    "sits below a title block), concatenates them, pivots to `(dates × companies)` price and\n",
    "volume matrices, keeps the `n_assets` most complete tickers, and forward/back-fills the\n",
    "remaining gaps. Results are cached to `data/processed/*.parquet`, so re-runs are fast.\n",
    "\n",
    "The parquet cache needs **`pyarrow`** (or `fastparquet`) installed. Without it the loader\n",
    "logs `Could not save cache (continuing)` and re-parses the CSVs on every run — harmless,\n",
    "just slower. `pip install pyarrow` to silence it.\n",
    "\n",
    "The loader expects one file per year in `YEAR_FILENAMES`. If a year is missing it raises;\n",
    "the cell below drops missing years instead, so a partial dataset still runs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-12",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "loader = CSEDataLoader(raw_data_dir=DATA_RAW_DIR)\n",
    "\n",
    "missing = {y: f for y, f in CSEDataLoader.YEAR_FILENAMES.items()\n",
    "           if not (Path(DATA_RAW_DIR) / f).exists()}\n",
    "if missing:\n",
    "    print(f\"Missing yearly files, dropping them: {list(missing.values())}\")\n",
    "    # Instance attribute shadows the class default for this loader only.\n",
    "    loader.YEAR_FILENAMES = {y: f for y, f in CSEDataLoader.YEAR_FILENAMES.items()\n",
    "                             if y not in missing}\n",
    "    print(\"NOTE: the parquet cache key ignores the year set — set FORCE_RELOAD = True \"\n",
    "          \"if you changed which years are present.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "prices, volumes = loader.load_prices_and_volumes(\n",
    "    n_assets=config.data.n_assets,\n",
    "    force_reload=FORCE_RELOAD,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "requested = config.data.n_assets\n",
    "config.data.asset_names = list(prices.columns)\n",
    "config.data.n_assets = len(config.data.asset_names)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nPrices  : {prices.shape}   {prices.index.min().date()} → {prices.index.max().date()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Volumes : {volumes.shape}\")\n",
    "if config.data.n_assets < requested:\n",
    "    print(f\"Requested {requested} assets; the sector file only holds {config.data.n_assets}.\")\n",
    "print(f\"Assets  : {config.data.asset_names}\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-13",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# ── Quick look at the universe ─────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 4.2))\n",
    "\n",
    "norm_prices = prices / prices.iloc[0]\n",
    "axes[0].plot(norm_prices.index, norm_prices.values, color=SERIES[0], alpha=0.30, lw=0.9)\n",
    "axes[0].plot(norm_prices.index, norm_prices.mean(axis=1), color=INK, lw=2.0)\n",
    "axes[0].axhline(1.0, color=GRID, lw=1.0)\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(\"Normalized prices, base = 1.0\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[0].annotate(\"equal-weight mean\", xy=(norm_prices.index[-1], norm_prices.mean(axis=1).iloc[-1]),\n",
    "                 xytext=(-8, 10), textcoords=\"offset points\", ha=\"right\", color=INK, fontsize=9)\n",
    "axes[0].annotate(\"individual banks\", xy=(norm_prices.index[len(norm_prices) // 3],\n",
    "                                         norm_prices.iloc[len(norm_prices) // 3].max()),\n",
    "                 xytext=(0, 6), textcoords=\"offset points\", color=SERIES[0], fontsize=9)\n",
    "\n",
    "daily_ret = np.log(prices / prices.shift(1)).dropna()\n",
    "ann_vol = daily_ret.std() * np.sqrt(252)\n",
    "order = ann_vol.sort_values()\n",
    "axes[1].barh(order.index, order.values, color=SERIES[0], height=0.62)\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(\"Annualized volatility by asset\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_xlabel(\"σ (annualized)\")\n",
    "axes[1].grid(axis=\"y\", visible=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Cross-sectional σ spread : {ann_vol.min():.1%} ({ann_vol.idxmin()}) \"\n",
    "      f\"→ {ann_vol.max():.1%} ({ann_vol.idxmax()})   ratio {ann_vol.max()/ann_vol.min():.1f}x\")\n",
    "print(\"This spread is exactly what MarketEnvironment's volatility scaling corrects for \"\n",
    "      \"in long/short mode — see _compute_vol_scale().\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-14",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 5. Feature engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "The Preprocessing Module. Per asset it builds **15** features:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Family | Features | Count / asset |\n",
    "|--------|----------|---------------|\n",
    "| Log return | `ln(P_t / P_{t−1})` | 1 |\n",
    "| Realized volatility | 5 / 10 / 20-day rolling σ, annualized | 3 |\n",
    "| Momentum | 5 / 10 / 20-day rate of change | 3 |\n",
    "| RSI | 14-day | 1 |\n",
    "| MACD | line, signal, histogram (12/26/9) | 3 |\n",
    "| Bollinger | %B (20-day, 2σ) | 1 |\n",
    "| Volume | volume / rolling-mean ratio, 5 / 10 / 20-day | 3 |\n",
    "| | **Total** | **15** |\n",
    "\n",
    "`reorder_per_asset()` then rearranges the columns so each asset's 15 features are\n",
    "**contiguous and in identical order**:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "[A0_ret, A0_vol5, …, A0_volratio20,  A1_ret, …,  AN_volratio20]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "That layout is a hard requirement, not a nicety: the encoder reshapes the flat\n",
    "`(T, N·15)` matrix into `(T, N, 15)`. Interleaved columns would silently hand asset *i*'s\n",
    "features to asset *j* — no error, just a model learning from scrambled inputs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-15",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "preprocessor = Preprocessor(\n",
    "    window_size=config.data.window_size,\n",
    "    normalize_method=config.data.normalize_method,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "features_all = preprocessor.engineer_features(prices, volumes, macro_data=None)\n",
    "features_all = preprocessor.reorder_per_asset(features_all, config.data.asset_names)\n",
    "\n",
    "F_PER_ASSET = preprocessor.n_features_per_asset\n",
    "FEATURE_NAMES = [s if s else \"_logret\" for s in Preprocessor.PER_ASSET_SUFFIXES]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Re-align price/volume matrices to the surviving feature index\n",
    "prices = prices.loc[features_all.index]\n",
    "volumes = volumes.loc[features_all.index]\n",
    "\n",
    "n_features_total = features_all.shape[1]\n",
    "assert n_features_total == config.data.n_assets * F_PER_ASSET, (\n",
    "    f\"{n_features_total} columns != {config.data.n_assets} assets x {F_PER_ASSET} features\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verify the per-asset blocking really is contiguous — this is the assumption\n",
    "# the (T, N, F) reshape inside the encoder relies on.\n",
    "first_block = list(features_all.columns[:F_PER_ASSET])\n",
    "assert all(c.startswith(config.data.asset_names[0]) for c in first_block), first_block\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Timesteps        : {len(features_all)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Features         : {n_features_total} = {config.data.n_assets} assets x {F_PER_ASSET}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Date range       : {features_all.index.min().date()} → {features_all.index.max().date()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"NaNs             : {int(features_all.isna().sum().sum())}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nFirst asset's block ({config.data.asset_names[0]}):\")\n",
    "for c in first_block:\n",
    "    print(f\"   {c}\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-16",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 6. Chronological splits, normalization, windowing\n",
    "\n",
    "Three points that decide whether the results mean anything:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Chronological, not random.** Splits are contiguous in time — no shuffling.\n",
    "2. **The scaler is fit on train only.** Val and test go through `transform_normalize`, so\n",
    "   no distributional information leaks backwards.\n",
    "3. **Prices are aligned to window *end* dates.** Window `i` spans rows `[i, i+W)`; the\n",
    "   agent acts on the close of row `i+W−1` and earns the return from `i+W−1 → i+W`. No\n",
    "   lookahead.\n",
    "\n",
    "Note that each split is windowed *independently*, so no window ever straddles a split\n",
    "boundary — train and test share no rows at all."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-17",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "n_total = len(features_all)\n",
    "n_train = int(n_total * config.data.train_ratio)\n",
    "n_val   = int(n_total * config.data.val_ratio)\n",
    "\n",
    "features_train = features_all.iloc[:n_train]\n",
    "features_val   = features_all.iloc[n_train:n_train + n_val]\n",
    "features_test  = features_all.iloc[n_train + n_val:]\n",
    "\n",
    "prices_train = prices.loc[features_train.index]\n",
    "prices_val   = prices.loc[features_val.index]\n",
    "prices_test  = prices.loc[features_test.index]\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Normalize: FIT ON TRAIN ONLY ───────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "norm_train = preprocessor.fit_normalize(features_train)\n",
    "norm_val   = preprocessor.transform_normalize(features_val)\n",
    "norm_test  = preprocessor.transform_normalize(features_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Sliding windows → x_t ──────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "windows_train = preprocessor.create_windows(norm_train.values)\n",
    "windows_val   = preprocessor.create_windows(norm_val.values)\n",
    "windows_test  = preprocessor.create_windows(norm_test.values)\n",
    "\n",
    "W = config.data.window_size\n",
    "prices_train_aligned = prices_train.iloc[W - 1:].values\n",
    "prices_val_aligned   = prices_val.iloc[W - 1:].values\n",
    "prices_test_aligned  = prices_test.iloc[W - 1:].values\n",
    "\n",
    "dates_train = features_train.index[W - 1:]\n",
    "dates_val   = features_val.index[W - 1:]\n",
    "dates_test  = features_test.index[W - 1:]\n",
    "\n",
    "split_table = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"rows\":    [len(features_train), len(features_val), len(features_test)],\n",
    "    \"windows\": [len(windows_train), len(windows_val), len(windows_test)],\n",
    "    \"start\":   [d[0].date()  for d in (dates_train, dates_val, dates_test)],\n",
    "    \"end\":     [d[-1].date() for d in (dates_train, dates_val, dates_test)],\n",
    "}, index=[\"train\", \"val\", \"test\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(split_table.to_string(), \"\\n\")\n",
    "print(f\"Observation x_t (flat)     : {windows_train.shape[1:]}   (window_size, n_assets*n_features)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Observation x_t (per-asset): ({config.data.n_assets}, {W}, {F_PER_ASSET})\"\n",
    "      \"   ← what the encoder reshapes it to\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-18",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 7. Market environments\n",
    "\n",
    "`MarketEnvironment` applies the actor's allocation, charges transaction costs and\n",
    "slippage on turnover, and tracks portfolio value. One instance per split.\n",
    "\n",
    "In long/short mode it also scales the raw per-asset signal by *relative* inverse\n",
    "volatility before clipping (DeePM Eq. 11), because the actor only ever sees z-scored\n",
    "features and so has no way to know that one bank is 10× riskier than another. In the\n",
    "long-only configuration used here that scaling is inactive — softmax weights are already\n",
    "a budget-constrained allocation, not a signal to rescale."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-19",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "def make_env(prices_arr, windows_arr):\n",
    "    return MarketEnvironment(\n",
    "        prices=prices_arr,\n",
    "        features=windows_arr,\n",
    "        initial_value=config.environment.initial_portfolio_value,\n",
    "        transaction_cost_rate=config.reward.transaction_cost_rate,\n",
    "        slippage=config.environment.slippage,\n",
    "        allow_short=config.environment.allow_short_selling,\n",
    "        max_position_size=config.environment.max_position_size,\n",
    "        vol_target=config.environment.vol_target,\n",
    "        vol_ewma_span=config.environment.vol_ewma_span,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "train_env = make_env(prices_train_aligned, windows_train)\n",
    "val_env   = make_env(prices_val_aligned,   windows_val)\n",
    "test_env  = make_env(prices_test_aligned,  windows_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "for name, env in [(\"train\", train_env), (\"val\", val_env), (\"test\", test_env)]:\n",
    "    print(f\"{name:<6} tradable steps={env.n_steps:<5} assets={env.n_assets}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nInitial capital     : LKR {config.environment.initial_portfolio_value:,.0f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Cost per unit turnover : {config.reward.transaction_cost_rate:.2%} fee \"\n",
    "      f\"+ {config.environment.slippage:.2%} slippage\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-20",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 8. Model construction\n",
    "\n",
    "`PPOAgent` wires the Differentiable Regime Encoder to the Actor and the Critic. Note the\n",
    "asymmetry: the **actor** consumes `h_asset` (one embedding per asset, shared-weight\n",
    "trunk, one logit each), while the **critic** and the regime classifier consume the\n",
    "mean-pooled `h_market` — a scalar value estimate and a market-level regime label are both\n",
    "market-wide concepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-21",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "set_seed(SEED)\n",
    "\n",
    "agent = PPOAgent(\n",
    "    n_features_per_asset=F_PER_ASSET,\n",
    "    n_assets=config.data.n_assets,\n",
    "    n_macro=config.data.n_macro_variables,          # 0 for this phase\n",
    "    vsn_hidden_dim=config.regime_encoder.vsn_hidden_dim,\n",
    "    lstm_hidden_dim=config.regime_encoder.lstm_hidden_dim,\n",
    "    lstm_num_layers=config.regime_encoder.lstm_num_layers,\n",
    "    mha_num_heads=config.regime_encoder.mha_num_heads,\n",
    "    gnn_hidden_dim=config.regime_encoder.gnn_hidden_dim,\n",
    "    gnn_num_heads=config.regime_encoder.gnn_num_heads,\n",
    "    gnn_num_layers=config.regime_encoder.gnn_num_layers,\n",
    "    n_regimes=config.regime_encoder.n_regimes,\n",
    "    latent_state_dim=config.regime_encoder.latent_state_dim,\n",
    "    actor_hidden_dims=config.actor.hidden_dims,\n",
    "    critic_hidden_dims=config.critic.hidden_dims,\n",
    "    encoder_dropout=config.regime_encoder.lstm_dropout,\n",
    "    mha_dropout=config.regime_encoder.mha_dropout,\n",
    "    actor_dropout=config.actor.dropout,\n",
    "    critic_dropout=config.critic.dropout,\n",
    "    allow_short=config.environment.allow_short_selling,\n",
    ").to(DEVICE)\n",
    "\n",
    "counts = agent.count_parameters()\n",
    "print(\"Trainable parameters\")\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 42)\n",
    "for k, v in counts.items():\n",
    "    if k == \"total\":\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    print(f\"  {k:<16} {v:>12,}   {v / counts['total'] * 100:5.1f}%\")\n",
    "print(\"-\" * 42)\n",
    "print(f\"  {'total':<16} {counts['total']:>12,}\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-22",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 8.1 Shape smoke test\n",
    "\n",
    "Verifies every tensor in the forward pass before committing to a training run — cheaper\n",
    "than discovering a shape bug forty minutes into training.\n",
    "\n",
    "It also checks the two input layouts are **equivalent**: the encoder accepts either the\n",
    "flat `(B, T, N·F)` windows the environment emits or an explicit `(B, N, T, F)` tensor,\n",
    "and the flat path must reshape to exactly the same thing."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-23",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "agent.eval()\n",
    "\n",
    "B = 4\n",
    "flat = torch.FloatTensor(windows_train[:B]).to(DEVICE)                    # (B, T, N*F)\n",
    "per_asset = flat.view(B, W, config.data.n_assets, F_PER_ASSET).permute(0, 2, 1, 3)\n",
    "\n",
    "with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "    out = agent(flat)\n",
    "    out_per_asset = agent(per_asset)\n",
    "\n",
    "N, R, L = config.data.n_assets, config.regime_encoder.n_regimes, config.regime_encoder.latent_state_dim\n",
    "expected = {\n",
    "    \"action\":        (B, N),\n",
    "    \"raw_action\":    (B, N),\n",
    "    \"log_prob\":      (B,),\n",
    "    \"entropy\":       (B,),\n",
    "    \"value\":         (B,),\n",
    "    \"h_asset\":       (B, N, L),\n",
    "    \"h_market\":      (B, L),\n",
    "    \"regime_probs\":  (B, R),\n",
    "    \"regime_logits\": (B, R),\n",
    "    \"var_weights\":   (B, N, W, F_PER_ASSET),\n",
    "    \"attn_weights\":  (B, N, config.regime_encoder.mha_num_heads, W, W),\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"input x_t : flat {tuple(flat.shape)}  ==  per-asset {tuple(per_asset.shape)}\\n\")\n",
    "all_ok = True\n",
    "for key, exp in expected.items():\n",
    "    got = tuple(out[key].shape)\n",
    "    ok = got == exp\n",
    "    all_ok &= ok\n",
    "    print(f\"  {'ok ' if ok else 'BAD'} {key:<14} {str(got):<26} expected {exp}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "same = torch.allclose(out[\"h_asset\"], out_per_asset[\"h_asset\"], atol=1e-5)\n",
    "print(f\"\\nflat and per-asset inputs agree : {same}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "w = out[\"action\"].cpu().numpy()\n",
    "if config.environment.allow_short_selling:\n",
    "    print(f\"weights in [-1, 1]  : {bool((np.abs(w) <= 1.0).all())}   (independent tanh, no budget constraint)\")\n",
    "    print(f\"gross exposure      : {np.abs(w).sum(axis=1).round(4)}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"weights sum to 1    : {np.allclose(w.sum(axis=1), 1.0)}   (row sums {w.sum(axis=1).round(6)})\")\n",
    "    print(f\"weights >= 0        : {bool((w >= 0).all())}\")\n",
    "print(f\"regime probs sum    : {out['regime_probs'].sum(dim=1).cpu().numpy().round(6)}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "assert all_ok and same, \"Shape mismatch — stop and investigate before training.\"\n",
    "print(\"\\nAll shape checks passed.\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-24",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 9. Training\n",
    "\n",
    "One PPO iteration:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Collect rollout** — step the policy through `train_env` for `rollout_length` steps,\n",
    "   recording observations, the **raw pre-squash actions**, log-probs, values and rewards.\n",
    "2. **Reward** — `rolling Sharpe(20d, annualized) − EVaR penalty − (linear + quadratic\n",
    "   turnover cost)`, from `RewardCalculator`.\n",
    "3. **Normalize + GAE(λ)** — rewards are scaled to unit discounted-return std (so the\n",
    "   critic's gradient doesn't monopolize the shared grad-norm clip), then\n",
    "   `δ_t = r_t + γV(s_{t+1}) − V(s_t)` accumulated backwards.\n",
    "4. **Update** — `L = L_clip + 0.5·L_value + 0.01·L_entropy`, backpropagated jointly\n",
    "   through encoder, actor and critic, gradient norm clipped at 0.5.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why the rollout stores `raw_action` and not the portfolio weights:** the policy density\n",
    "is defined over the pre-squash Gaussian sample. Storing the softmax output and\n",
    "re-evaluating *that* under the Gaussian would make `exp(new − old)` a ratio between two\n",
    "different random variables — not an importance weight, and the clipping would be\n",
    "operating on a meaningless number. `PPOAgent.forward()` returns both; the trainer keeps\n",
    "`raw_action` for the ratio and sends `action` to the environment.\n",
    "\n",
    "**No LSTM state is carried across rollout steps.** Each observation is already a complete\n",
    "30-day window, and `evaluate_actions()` re-encodes with a fresh hidden state during the\n",
    "update. Carrying hidden state during collection would make the stored `log_prob` refer to\n",
    "a different state than the one re-evaluated at update time. Evaluation below matches this."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-25",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "run_id  = datetime.now().strftime(\"%Y%m%d_%H%M%S\")\n",
    "log_dir = os.path.join(LOGS_DIR, f\"nb_{run_id}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "trainer = PPOTrainer(\n",
    "    agent=agent,\n",
    "    train_env=train_env,\n",
    "    val_env=val_env,\n",
    "    clip_epsilon=config.ppo.clip_epsilon,\n",
    "    gamma=config.ppo.gamma,\n",
    "    gae_lambda=config.ppo.gae_lambda,\n",
    "    entropy_coeff=config.ppo.entropy_coeff,\n",
    "    value_loss_coeff=config.ppo.value_loss_coeff,\n",
    "    learning_rate=config.ppo.learning_rate,\n",
    "    max_grad_norm=config.ppo.max_grad_norm,\n",
    "    batch_size=config.ppo.batch_size,\n",
    "    n_epochs=config.ppo.n_epochs,\n",
    "    rollout_length=config.ppo.rollout_length,\n",
    "    total_timesteps=config.ppo.total_timesteps,\n",
    "    eval_frequency=config.ppo.eval_frequency,\n",
    "    save_frequency=config.ppo.save_frequency,\n",
    "    early_stopping_patience=config.ppo.early_stopping_patience,\n",
    "    log_dir=log_dir,\n",
    "    save_dir=MODELS_DIR,\n",
    "    device=DEVICE,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"run id       : {run_id}\")\n",
    "print(f\"tensorboard  : {log_dir}\")\n",
    "print(f\"checkpoints  : {MODELS_DIR}\")\n",
    "print(f\"rollouts     : {config.ppo.total_timesteps // config.ppo.rollout_length}\")\n",
    "print(f\"grad steps   : ~{config.ppo.total_timesteps // config.ppo.rollout_length * config.ppo.n_epochs * max(1, config.ppo.rollout_length // config.ppo.batch_size):,}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nCheckpoints are written to the SHARED models dir — best_model.pt from a previous \"\n",
    "      \"run will be overwritten once this run beats its own best validation Sharpe.\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-26",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "%%time\n",
    "set_seed(SEED)\n",
    "history = trainer.train()\n",
    "print(\"\\nTraining complete.\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-27",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 9.1 Training curves\n",
    "\n",
    "`approx_kl` and `clip_fraction` are the two to watch. A clip fraction that pins near 1.0\n",
    "means the policy is trying to move much further than `clip_epsilon` allows every update —\n",
    "usually too high a learning rate. A KL that collapses to ~0 means the policy has stopped\n",
    "moving at all."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-28",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "hist = history[\"history\"] if isinstance(history, dict) and \"history\" in history else history\n",
    "hist_df = pd.DataFrame(hist)\n",
    "\n",
    "panels = [\n",
    "    (\"total_loss\",    \"Total loss\"),\n",
    "    (\"policy_loss\",   \"Policy loss (L_clip)\"),\n",
    "    (\"value_loss\",    \"Value loss (MSE)\"),\n",
    "    (\"entropy_loss\",  \"Entropy loss\"),\n",
    "    (\"approx_kl\",     \"Approx. KL\"),\n",
    "    (\"clip_fraction\", \"Clip fraction\"),\n",
    "    (\"avg_reward\",    \"Mean rollout reward\"),\n",
    "]\n",
    "available = [(k, t) for k, t in panels if k in hist_df.columns]\n",
    "\n",
    "if available:\n",
    "    ncols = 3\n",
    "    nrows = int(np.ceil(len(available) / ncols))\n",
    "    fig, axes = plt.subplots(nrows, ncols, figsize=(14, 3.4 * nrows), squeeze=False)\n",
    "    axes = axes.ravel()\n",
    "    for ax, (key, title) in zip(axes, available):\n",
    "        y = hist_df[key].to_numpy(dtype=float)\n",
    "        ax.plot(hist_df[\"step\"], y, lw=1.4, color=SERIES[0], alpha=0.55)\n",
    "        if len(y) >= 10:\n",
    "            k = max(3, len(y) // 12)\n",
    "            ma = np.convolve(y, np.ones(k) / k, mode=\"valid\")\n",
    "            ax.plot(hist_df[\"step\"].to_numpy()[k - 1:], ma, lw=2.0, color=SERIES[1])\n",
    "            ax.annotate(f\"MA({k})\", xy=(hist_df[\"step\"].iloc[-1], ma[-1]),\n",
    "                        xytext=(-4, 6), textcoords=\"offset points\",\n",
    "                        ha=\"right\", color=SERIES[1], fontsize=8)\n",
    "        ax.set_title(title, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "        ax.set_xlabel(\"timestep\")\n",
    "    for ax in axes[len(available):]:\n",
    "        ax.axis(\"off\")\n",
    "    plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(hist_df[[c for c, _ in available]].describe().loc[[\"mean\", \"std\", \"min\", \"max\"]].to_string())\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"trainer.train() returned no per-update history. Full record in TensorBoard:\")\n",
    "    print(f\"  %load_ext tensorboard\\n  %tensorboard --logdir {log_dir}\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-29",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 10. Evaluation & backtest\n",
    "\n",
    "`run_episode` walks an environment deterministically (policy mean, no sampling) and\n",
    "records everything needed for analysis: portfolio values, weights, regime probabilities,\n",
    "variable-selection weights and attention maps.\n",
    "\n",
    "Two details it gets right that a naive loop would not:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Fresh LSTM state per window**, matching `collect_rollout` and `evaluate` in the\n",
    "  trainer. Carrying it here would evaluate a different model than the one trained.\n",
    "- **Turnover is computed from `weight_history`, not from `info[\"turnover\"]`.** In\n",
    "  `market_env.py:272` the info field is computed *after* `self.current_weights` has\n",
    "  already been reassigned to `new_weights`, so it is identically zero. Training is\n",
    "  unaffected (the trainer captures `old_weights` separately for the reward), but any\n",
    "  turnover number taken from `info` would be wrong."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-30",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "@torch.no_grad()\n",
    "def run_episode(agent, env, device=DEVICE, deterministic=True, capture_internals=True):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Roll a policy through an environment; return a dict of trajectories.\"\"\"\n",
    "    agent.eval()\n",
    "    obs = env.reset()\n",
    "    done = False\n",
    "\n",
    "    regime_probs, values, attn_maps, var_maps = [], [], [], []\n",
    "\n",
    "    while not done:\n",
    "        x = torch.FloatTensor(obs[\"features\"]).unsqueeze(0).to(device)\n",
    "        # lstm_hidden intentionally NOT carried — matches training.\n",
    "        out = agent(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n",
    "\n",
    "        regime_probs.append(out[\"regime_probs\"].cpu().numpy()[0])\n",
    "        values.append(float(out[\"value\"].cpu().item()))\n",
    "        if capture_internals:\n",
    "            # attn: (1, N, heads, T, T) → mean over assets and heads → (T, T)\n",
    "            attn_maps.append(out[\"attn_weights\"].mean(dim=(1, 2)).cpu().numpy()[0])\n",
    "            # var:  (1, N, T, F)        → mean over assets and time  → (F,)\n",
    "            var_maps.append(out[\"var_weights\"].mean(dim=(1, 2)).cpu().numpy()[0])\n",
    "\n",
    "        action = out[\"action\"].cpu().numpy()[0]\n",
    "        next_obs, _, done, _ = env.step(action)\n",
    "        if next_obs is None:\n",
    "            break\n",
    "        obs = next_obs\n",
    "\n",
    "    weights = np.asarray(env.weight_history, dtype=float)\n",
    "    turnover = np.abs(np.diff(weights, axis=0)).sum(axis=1)   # see note above\n",
    "\n",
    "    return {\n",
    "        \"portfolio_values\": np.asarray(env.portfolio_history, dtype=float),\n",
    "        \"returns\":          np.asarray(env.return_history, dtype=float),\n",
    "        \"weights\":          weights,\n",
    "        \"costs\":            np.asarray(env.cost_history, dtype=float),\n",
    "        \"turnover\":         turnover,\n",
    "        \"regime_probs\":     np.asarray(regime_probs, dtype=float),\n",
    "        \"values\":           np.asarray(values, dtype=float),\n",
    "        \"attention\":        np.asarray(attn_maps, dtype=float) if attn_maps else None,\n",
    "        \"var_weights\":      np.asarray(var_maps, dtype=float) if var_maps else None,\n",
    "        \"summary\":          env.get_performance_summary(),\n",
    "    }\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"run_episode defined.\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-31",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# ── Load the best checkpoint if the trainer saved one ──────────────────\n",
    "best_ckpt = os.path.join(MODELS_DIR, \"best_model.pt\")\n",
    "if os.path.exists(best_ckpt):\n",
    "    trainer.load_checkpoint(best_ckpt)\n",
    "    print(f\"Loaded best checkpoint: {best_ckpt}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"No best_model.pt found — evaluating the final in-memory weights.\\n\"\n",
    "          \"(If training was shorter than eval_frequency, evaluation never ran.)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Run all three splits ───────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "episodes = {}\n",
    "for name, env in [(\"train\", train_env), (\"val\", val_env), (\"test\", test_env)]:\n",
    "    episodes[name] = run_episode(agent, env)\n",
    "    s = episodes[name][\"summary\"]\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n{name.upper():<6} total_return={s['total_return']:+.4f}  \"\n",
    "          f\"sharpe={s['sharpe_ratio']:+.3f}  max_dd={s['max_drawdown']:.4f}  \"\n",
    "          f\"final=LKR {s['final_portfolio_value']:,.0f}\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-32",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 10.1 Full metric suite\n",
    "\n",
    "`PortfolioMetrics` adds Sortino, Calmar, VaR / CVaR / EVaR, win rate and profit factor on\n",
    "top of the environment's own summary.\n",
    "\n",
    "Expect train to look better than test. If it doesn't, something is wrong upstream rather\n",
    "than the model being unusually honest."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-33",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "metrics_calc = PortfolioMetrics(risk_free_rate=config.reward.risk_free_rate)\n",
    "\n",
    "METRIC_ORDER = [\n",
    "    \"total_return\", \"annualized_return\", \"annualized_volatility\",\n",
    "    \"sharpe_ratio\", \"sortino_ratio\", \"calmar_ratio\", \"max_drawdown\",\n",
    "    \"var_95\", \"cvar_95\", \"evar_95\", \"win_rate\", \"profit_factor\", \"final_value\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "metrics_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    name: metrics_calc.compute_all(res[\"returns\"], res[\"portfolio_values\"])\n",
    "    for name, res in episodes.items()\n",
    "}).reindex(METRIC_ORDER)\n",
    "\n",
    "pd.set_option(\"display.float_format\", lambda v: f\"{v:,.4f}\")\n",
    "metrics_df"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-34",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 11. Benchmarks\n",
    "\n",
    "An RL portfolio result means nothing without a baseline. Two cheap, honest ones on the\n",
    "same test prices, with the same cost model:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Equal-weight buy & hold** — `1/N` on day one, never rebalanced. No turnover, so no\n",
    "  costs after entry.\n",
    "- **Equal-weight daily rebalance** — reset to `1/N` every day, paying the agent's\n",
    "  transaction-cost and slippage rates. This is the one that shows what the cost drag of\n",
    "  daily trading actually is.\n",
    "\n",
    "If the agent can't beat these on the **test** split, there is no result to report."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-35",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "def buy_and_hold(prices_arr, initial_value):\n",
    "    w0 = np.ones(prices_arr.shape[1]) / prices_arr.shape[1]\n",
    "    shares = initial_value * w0 / (prices_arr[0] + 1e-10)\n",
    "    pv = (shares[None, :] * prices_arr).sum(axis=1)\n",
    "    return pv, pv[1:] / pv[:-1] - 1.0\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def equal_weight_rebalanced(prices_arr, initial_value, tc_rate, slippage):\n",
    "    n = prices_arr.shape[1]\n",
    "    target = np.ones(n) / n\n",
    "    pv, w = initial_value, np.zeros(n)\n",
    "    values, rets = [pv], []\n",
    "    for t in range(len(prices_arr) - 1):\n",
    "        turnover = np.abs(target - w).sum()\n",
    "        cost = (tc_rate + slippage) * turnover * pv\n",
    "        r = float(np.dot(target, (prices_arr[t + 1] - prices_arr[t]) / (prices_arr[t] + 1e-10)))\n",
    "        pv = pv * (1 + r) - cost\n",
    "        w = target\n",
    "        values.append(pv); rets.append(r)\n",
    "    return np.asarray(values), np.asarray(rets)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "init_val = config.environment.initial_portfolio_value\n",
    "res = episodes[\"test\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Benchmarks run over exactly the steps the agent traded.\n",
    "n_steps_agent = len(res[\"portfolio_values\"])\n",
    "bench_prices = prices_test_aligned[:n_steps_agent]\n",
    "\n",
    "bh_values, bh_returns = buy_and_hold(bench_prices, init_val)\n",
    "ew_values, ew_returns = equal_weight_rebalanced(\n",
    "    bench_prices, init_val,\n",
    "    config.reward.transaction_cost_rate, config.environment.slippage,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "BENCH_LABELS = [\"PPO agent\", \"Equal-wt buy & hold\", \"Equal-wt rebalanced\"]\n",
    "comparison = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    BENCH_LABELS[0]: metrics_calc.compute_all(res[\"returns\"], res[\"portfolio_values\"]),\n",
    "    BENCH_LABELS[1]: metrics_calc.compute_all(bh_returns, bh_values),\n",
    "    BENCH_LABELS[2]: metrics_calc.compute_all(ew_returns, ew_values),\n",
    "}).reindex(METRIC_ORDER)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"TEST SPLIT — {n_steps_agent} trading days, \"\n",
    "      f\"{dates_test[0].date()} → {dates_test[min(n_steps_agent, len(dates_test)) - 1].date()}\\n\")\n",
    "comparison"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-36",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 12. Visualization\n",
    "\n",
    "### 12.1 Equity curve and drawdown"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-37",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "pv = res[\"portfolio_values\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 1, figsize=(13, 7.5), sharex=True,\n",
    "                         gridspec_kw={\"height_ratios\": [3, 1]})\n",
    "\n",
    "curves = [(pv, BENCH_LABELS[0], SERIES[0], 2.2),\n",
    "          (bh_values, BENCH_LABELS[1], SERIES[1], 1.6),\n",
    "          (ew_values, BENCH_LABELS[2], SERIES[2], 1.6)]\n",
    "\n",
    "for series, label, colour, lw in curves:\n",
    "    axes[0].plot(series, lw=lw, color=colour, label=label)\n",
    "    axes[0].annotate(label, xy=(len(series) - 1, series[-1]), xytext=(6, 0),\n",
    "                     textcoords=\"offset points\", va=\"center\", color=colour, fontsize=9)\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[0].axhline(init_val, color=GRID, ls=\"--\", lw=1.0)\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Portfolio value (LKR)\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(\"Test-split equity curve\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[0].legend(loc=\"upper left\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlim(0, len(pv) * 1.16)\n",
    "\n",
    "peak = np.maximum.accumulate(pv)\n",
    "dd = (peak - pv) / (peak + 1e-10)\n",
    "axes[1].fill_between(range(len(dd)), dd, color=SERIES[0], alpha=0.35, lw=0)\n",
    "axes[1].plot(dd, color=SERIES[0], lw=1.2)\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel(\"Drawdown\"); axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Trading day\")\n",
    "axes[1].invert_yaxis()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Agent final   : LKR {pv[-1]:,.0f}  ({pv[-1]/init_val - 1:+.2%})\")\n",
    "print(f\"Buy & hold    : LKR {bh_values[-1]:,.0f}  ({bh_values[-1]/init_val - 1:+.2%})\")\n",
    "print(f\"EW rebalanced : LKR {ew_values[-1]:,.0f}  ({ew_values[-1]/init_val - 1:+.2%})\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-38",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 12.2 Learned regimes\n",
    "\n",
    "The regime classifier is trained **without labels** — nothing anchors index 0 to \"bull\".\n",
    "They are numbered, not named, and the colours are plain categorical slots: assigning\n",
    "green/red would assert a semantics the model was never given. Read the entropy panel\n",
    "first — if it sits near `ln(3) ≈ 1.099` the classifier is emitting near-uniform\n",
    "probabilities and is not separating anything, which would sink the \"regime detection\"\n",
    "claim regardless of how the equity curve looks."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-39",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "rp = res[\"regime_probs\"]\n",
    "n_reg = rp.shape[1]\n",
    "regime_names = [f\"Regime {i}\" for i in range(n_reg)]\n",
    "regime_colors = (SERIES * ((n_reg // len(SERIES)) + 1))[:n_reg]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(3, 1, figsize=(13, 9), sharex=True,\n",
    "                         gridspec_kw={\"height_ratios\": [2, 2, 1.4]})\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[0].stackplot(range(len(rp)), rp.T, labels=regime_names,\n",
    "                  colors=regime_colors, alpha=0.85, edgecolor=\"#fcfcfb\", linewidth=0.5)\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel(\"P(regime)\"); axes[0].set_ylim(0, 1)\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(\"Latent regime probabilities — learned end-to-end, no regime labels\",\n",
    "                  fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "axes[0].legend(loc=\"upper right\", ncol=n_reg)\n",
    "axes[0].grid(visible=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "pv_r = pv[:len(rp)]\n",
    "axes[1].plot(pv_r, lw=1.8, color=INK)\n",
    "dominant = rp.argmax(axis=1)\n",
    "for k, c in enumerate(regime_colors):\n",
    "    axes[1].fill_between(range(len(rp)), pv_r.min(), pv_r.max(),\n",
    "                         where=(dominant == k), color=c, alpha=0.16, lw=0)\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel(\"Portfolio value\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(\"Equity curve shaded by dominant regime\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ent = -(rp * np.log(rp + 1e-10)).sum(axis=1)\n",
    "axes[2].plot(ent, lw=1.4, color=SERIES[0])\n",
    "axes[2].axhline(np.log(n_reg), color=INK_MUTED, ls=\"--\", lw=1.0)\n",
    "axes[2].annotate(f\"max = ln({n_reg}) = {np.log(n_reg):.3f}\", xy=(0, np.log(n_reg)),\n",
    "                 xytext=(4, -12), textcoords=\"offset points\", color=INK_MUTED, fontsize=9)\n",
    "axes[2].set_ylabel(\"Regime entropy\"); axes[2].set_xlabel(\"Trading day\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "occupancy = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"mean P\": rp.mean(axis=0),\n",
    "    \"days dominant\": [int((dominant == k).sum()) for k in range(n_reg)],\n",
    "    \"share of days\": [(dominant == k).mean() for k in range(n_reg)],\n",
    "}, index=regime_names)\n",
    "print(occupancy.to_string(float_format=lambda v: f\"{v:.4f}\"), \"\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "verdict = (\"confident, well-separated regimes\" if ent.mean() < 0.8 * np.log(n_reg)\n",
    "           else \"NEAR-UNIFORM — the regimes are not separating; do not claim regime detection\")\n",
    "print(f\"Mean entropy {ent.mean():.4f} / max {np.log(n_reg):.4f}   → {verdict}\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-40",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 12.3 Allocation behaviour"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
