  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-42",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 12.4 What the encoder attends to\n",
    "\n",
    "Two interpretability views, both averaged over the test episode:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Temporal attention** — which days inside the 30-day window the decision timestep\n",
    "  looks at. Only the last query row reaches `h_temp` (`regime_encoder.py:160`), so that\n",
    "  row is the one that matters.\n",
    "- **Variable selection** — which of the 15 per-asset features the VSN gates open for.\n",
    "  A flat profile means the VSN is not selecting; that is a finding, not a bug to hide."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-43",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(15, 4.2), gridspec_kw={\"width_ratios\": [1, 1.1, 1.2]})\n",
    "\n",
    "if res[\"attention\"] is not None:\n",
    "    attn = res[\"attention\"]                       # (T_steps, W, W)\n",
    "    im = axes[0].imshow(attn.mean(axis=0), cmap=\"Blues\", aspect=\"auto\", origin=\"lower\")\n",
    "    axes[0].set_xlabel(\"Key timestep\"); axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Query timestep\")\n",
    "    axes[0].set_title(\"Mean attention map\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "    axes[0].grid(visible=False)\n",
    "    plt.colorbar(im, ax=axes[0])\n",
    "\n",
    "    last_row = attn[:, -1, :].mean(axis=0)\n",
    "    axes[1].bar(range(len(last_row)), last_row, color=SERIES[0], width=0.72)\n",
    "    axes[1].axhline(1 / len(last_row), color=SERIES[1], ls=\"--\", lw=1.4)\n",
    "    axes[1].annotate(f\"uniform = {1/len(last_row):.3f}\", xy=(0, 1 / len(last_row)),\n",
    "                     xytext=(2, 5), textcoords=\"offset points\", color=SERIES[1], fontsize=9)\n",
    "    axes[1].set_xlabel(f\"Day in window (0 = oldest, {len(last_row)-1} = decision day)\")\n",
    "    axes[1].set_ylabel(\"Attention weight\")\n",
    "    axes[1].set_title(\"Attention from the decision timestep\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "    axes[1].grid(axis=\"x\", visible=False)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    axes[0].axis(\"off\"); axes[1].axis(\"off\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if res[\"var_weights\"] is not None:\n",
    "    vw = res[\"var_weights\"].mean(axis=0)           # (F,)\n",
    "    order_v = np.argsort(vw)\n",
    "    axes[2].barh([FEATURE_NAMES[i] for i in order_v], vw[order_v], color=SERIES[0], height=0.66)\n",
    "    axes[2].axvline(1 / len(vw), color=SERIES[1], ls=\"--\", lw=1.4)\n",
    "    axes[2].set_xlabel(\"Mean VSN weight\")\n",
    "    axes[2].set_title(\"Variable selection (per-asset features)\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "    axes[2].tick_params(labelsize=8)\n",
    "    axes[2].grid(axis=\"y\", visible=False)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    axes[2].axis(\"off\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "if res[\"attention\"] is not None:\n",
    "    lr = attn[:, -1, :].mean(axis=0)\n",
    "    print(\"Most-attended days in the window:\")\n",
    "    for i in np.argsort(lr)[::-1][:5]:\n",
    "        print(f\"   index {i:2d}  (t-{len(lr)-1-i:<2})  weight {lr[i]:.4f}\")\n",
    "if res[\"var_weights\"] is not None:\n",
    "    vw = res[\"var_weights\"].mean(axis=0)\n",
    "    print(\"\\nTop features by VSN weight:\")\n",
    "    for i in np.argsort(vw)[::-1][:5]:\n",
    "        print(f\"   {FEATURE_NAMES[i]:<16} {vw[i]:.4f}   (uniform = {1/len(vw):.4f})\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-44",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 13. Saving artifacts\n",
    "\n",
    "Everything needed to reproduce or write up this run goes to\n",
    "`results/nb_run_<run_id>/`, keyed by the same `run_id` as the TensorBoard directory."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "cell-45",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "out_dir = Path(RESULTS_DIR) / f\"nb_run_{run_id}\"\n",
    "out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Metrics\n",
    "metrics_df.to_csv(out_dir / \"metrics_by_split.csv\")\n",
    "comparison.to_csv(out_dir / \"test_vs_benchmarks.csv\")\n",
    "hist_df.to_csv(out_dir / \"training_history.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Per-step trajectory (test split)\n",
    "n_rows = len(res[\"portfolio_values\"])\n",
    "traj = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"date\": dates_test[:n_rows],\n",
    "    \"portfolio_value\": res[\"portfolio_values\"][:n_rows],\n",
    "})\n",
    "traj[\"portfolio_return\"] = np.r_[0.0, res[\"returns\"]][:n_rows]\n",
    "traj[\"cost\"]             = np.r_[0.0, res[\"costs\"]][:n_rows]\n",
    "traj[\"turnover\"]         = np.r_[0.0, res[\"turnover\"]][:n_rows]\n",
    "for k, nme in enumerate(regime_names):\n",
    "    traj[f\"p_regime_{k}\"] = np.r_[np.nan, rp[:, k]][:n_rows]\n",
    "for i, a in enumerate(asset_names):\n",
    "    traj[f\"w_{a}\"] = res[\"weights\"][:n_rows, i]\n",
    "traj.to_csv(out_dir / \"test_trajectory.csv\", index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Run manifest\n",
    "manifest = {\n",
    "    \"run_id\": run_id,\n",
    "    \"timestamp\": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n",
    "    \"seed\": SEED,\n",
    "    \"device\": DEVICE,\n",
    "    \"n_assets\": config.data.n_assets,\n",
    "    \"asset_names\": config.data.asset_names,\n",
    "    \"n_features_per_asset\": int(F_PER_ASSET),\n",
    "    \"window_size\": int(config.data.window_size),\n",
    "    \"allow_short\": bool(config.environment.allow_short_selling),\n",
    "    \"total_timesteps\": int(config.ppo.total_timesteps),\n",
    "    \"rollout_length\": int(config.ppo.rollout_length),\n",
    "    \"learning_rate\": float(config.ppo.learning_rate),\n",
    "    \"parameters\": counts,\n",
    "    \"splits\": {\"train\": len(windows_train), \"val\": len(windows_val), \"test\": len(windows_test)},\n",
    "    \"test_summary\": {k: float(v) for k, v in res[\"summary\"].items()},\n",
    "    \"mean_regime_entropy\": float(ent.mean()),\n",
    "}\n",
    "(out_dir / \"manifest.json\").write_text(json.dumps(manifest, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# 4. Model checkpoint\n",
    "torch.save({\"model_state_dict\": agent.state_dict(), \"manifest\": manifest},\n",
    "           out_dir / \"agent_final.pt\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Saved to {out_dir}\\n\")\n",
    "for p in sorted(out_dir.iterdir()):\n",
    "    print(f\"  {p.name:<26} {p.stat().st_size/1024:>10,.1f} KB\")"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-46",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Notes & next steps\n",
    "\n",
    "**Before reporting any number from this notebook:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Raise `TOTAL_TIMESTEPS`.** 20k exists so the notebook runs end-to-end in minutes. It\n",
    "   is far too short to converge.\n",
    "2. **Run multiple seeds.** Single-seed RL results are noise. Report mean ± std over at\n",
    "   least 5 seeds — change `SEED` in §2 and re-run.\n",
    "3. **Check the regime entropy panel (§12.2).** Near `ln(3)` means no regime separation,\n",
    "   and the central claim of the project is unsupported no matter what the equity curve did.\n",
    "4. **Beat the benchmarks in §11 on the *test* split.** Train performance is not evidence.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Known issues in the current source, in the order they matter:**\n",
    "\n",
    "| # | Issue | Where | Status |\n",
    "|---|-------|-------|--------|\n",
    "| 1 | `info[\"turnover\"]` is always 0 — `self.current_weights` is reassigned before the difference is taken | `src/environment/market_env.py:252,272` | Worked around in §10: turnover is recomputed from `weight_history`. Training and reward are unaffected. |\n",
    "| 2 | The softmax/tanh squash has no change-of-variables (Jacobian) correction in the log-prob | `src/models/actor.py` | The ratio is at least self-consistent — the raw pre-squash sample is stored and re-evaluated — which is the standard pragmatic treatment. Mention the approximation in the methods section. |\n",
    "| 3 | `DifferentiableReward` is defined but never used | `src/environment/reward.py` | Harmless, but don't claim gradients flow *through* the reward. In PPO they reach the encoder via the advantage only. |\n",
    "| 4 | Only the last MHA query row reaches `h_temp`, so 29/30 of the attention computation is discarded | `src/models/regime_encoder.py:160` | Correct, just wasteful. Attention pooling with one learnable query would be far cheaper. |\n",
    "| 5 | Checkpoints are shared across runs — `best_model.pt` is overwritten in place | `src/training/trainer.py` | Copy `results/models/best_model.pt` into the run directory if you need to keep it. |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Extending the notebook:**\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Macro variables.** Set `config.data.n_macro_variables > 0` and pass `macro_data` to\n",
    "  `engineer_features()`. Note that `reorder_per_asset()` rejects macro columns — they are\n",
    "  not per-asset — so the macro path needs a separate branch feeding the graph prior.\n",
    "- **Long/short.** Set `config.environment.allow_short_selling = True` in §3. The actor\n",
    "  switches to independent per-asset tanh and the environment's volatility scaling\n",
    "  activates. CSE short-selling/SBL availability is unverified — confirm before treating\n",
    "  those results as executable."
   ]
  }
